### LAYER 6 — Retrieval Pipeline (THE MOAT)

> *"This is what makes GitMem valuable. Not the database. The retrieval intelligence."*

```mermaid
graph TD
    classDef step fill:#e0f7fa,stroke:#00838f,stroke-width:2px
    classDef core fill:#fce4ec,stroke:#c2185b,stroke-width:3px

    Q["User Query"] --> RET["Retrieval Orchestrator"]:::core

    RET --> S1["1. Semantic Search\n(ChromaDB)"]:::step
    RET --> S2["2. Recency Retrieval\n(Supabase ORDER BY created_at)"]:::step
    RET --> S3["3. Importance Retrieval\n(Supabase ORDER BY importance)"]:::step
    RET --> S4["4. Episodic Retrieval\n(time-windowed events)"]:::step
    RET --> S5["5. Graph Traversal\n(related memories)"]:::step

    S1 --> MERGE["Candidate Pool\n(deduplicated)"]
    S2 --> MERGE
    S3 --> MERGE
    S4 --> MERGE
    S5 --> MERGE

    MERGE --> RERANK["6. Reranker\n(multi-signal scoring)"]:::core
    RERANK --> PACK["7. Token Packer\n(fit to budget)"]:::step
    PACK --> SUMM["8. Summarizer\n(compress if needed)"]:::step
    SUMM --> OUT["Context Window\n(ready for LLM)"]
```

**Scoring formula**:
```
score = (w1 × cosine_sim) + (w2 × recency_decay) + (w3 × importance) + (w4 × access_freq) + (w5 × scope_boost)
```

Weights are configurable per workspace/repo.

